{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~","id":1403985,"title":"Hello there Sir, can I get the consent paper for your sex slaves plz ~","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-22T06:01:24-07:00","id":1403985,"title":"Hello there Sir, can I get the consent paper for your sex slaves plz ~","content":"<img src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/498704231407288320/734801032051294225/image0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Isn't it weird that most of the OOC conversations around demons are how cool and fun demon-summoning is? Even though you are basically taking a POW and slaps a psychic collar on them.<br /> <br /> People arguing endlessly about the morality of the Abyssal when they promise to kill the world in exchange for power, but I haven't seen anything yet about the PCs being slaver that enjoys from the fruit of their ancestor's conquests. I guess this isn't a story-hook that Exalted is interested in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:16:49-07:00","id":1403986,"title":"","content":"What's a POW ? <br /> <br /> I think it's a complicated matter. I try to approach the world of Exalted as some kind of (fantasized) mythical Antique time of earth, where slaves was just a political situation among others, and not a central political matter.<br /> <br /> More generally in RPGs, I try to consider that, as long as I know that the person I'm playing with is not truly defending offensive political views in real life, all philosophies are more or less equal morally, the question being more how they will handle personal dilemma rather than questioning universal modern moral problematics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:17:15-07:00","id":1403987,"title":"","content":"Well, it depends on what your goals are.<br /> <br /> The game is primarily supposed to be fun, and it is set in a setting where there are many, many, <i>many</i> things that are cool to play that would be outright immoral irl, like your slavery example, murder, despotism and so on.<br /> <br /> So these things are there for you to question if that's what you want to do, but mostly the zeitgeist doesn't, and nor do most players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:22:55-07:00","id":1403988,"title":"","content":"Abyssals, more specifically, show up often because they take it an extra step, and are defined by it in both acceptance and rejection.<br /> <br /> An archetypal noble/degenerate scion of death won't exactly be chill and blend in the background of a world like Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:28:28-07:00","id":1403990,"title":"","content":"Talking about that, I'm rather curious to read a moral analysis from old greek/chinese philosophies of stories like the gods overthrowing the titans in the greek mythology, or the (possible) equivalents in other cosmologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:35:40-07:00","id":1403991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1403986#post1403986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's a POW ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prisoner of war, since the demon and their master lost the war against the god and are imprisoned right now (probably for all eternity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:39:38-07:00","id":1403994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1403991#post1403991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prisoner of war, since the demon and their master lost the war against the god and are imprisoned right now (probably for all eternity).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right. Maybe you could see d\u00e9mon summoning as some sort of Community Service for the bad people we put in prison because they were bad ? I wonder how would a sorcerer with an intimacy of &quot;Demons are just repaying for the harm they caused&quot; might play out in a game with lots of interactions with supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:46:01-07:00","id":1404000,"title":"","content":"That seems pretty \u201cChristianity Hell\u201d to me, I guess it would be fine for a character to feel like that? It\u2019s probably won\u2019t be what the book is going for though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:48:18-07:00","id":1404002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404000#post1404000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems pretty \u201cChristianity Hell\u201d to me, I guess it would be fine for a character to feel like that? It\u2019s probably won\u2019t be what the book is going for though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah most likely I don't see it appearing in a book but I find the idea behind the concept interesting. What's happening on your image ? I'm unsure who is who and doing what ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:52:02-07:00","id":1404005,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s been a thread or two about \u201cis it okay to enslave demons and/or elementals because that\u2019s what summoning is\u201d. Generally I think the topic is skipped over because most people don\u2019t judge demons as being the same thing as people. They\u2019re not human, have non-human drives and needs(some are close to human, some aren\u2019t), and so are thought of differently. Most traditions exalted draws on for its occultism take similar views on the morality of compelling demons to your service.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:54:43-07:00","id":1404006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404002#post1404002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah most likely I don't see it appearing in a book but I find the idea behind the concept interesting. What's happening on your image ? I'm unsure who is who and doing what ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just my Zenith summoning Octavian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T07:03:15-07:00","id":1404010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404006#post1404006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just my Zenith summoning Octavian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay but what's the little thing on the floor and why does it have an Exalted Caste Mark ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T07:04:25-07:00","id":1404011,"title":"","content":"The head of a Solar, he killed one long ago and wears it on his hip. Does his Ex3 write-up not mention this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T07:11:30-07:00","id":1404014,"title":"","content":"Oh that's what it is. I thought it was some sort of pet or companion or friend of your Zenith, so I didn't get it was actually a part of Octavian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T07:57:23-07:00","id":1404022,"title":"","content":"There was loads of conversation about this during Exalted's original run. It got downgraded a little bit I think as change in conversation / previous devs looking to emphasise more the heroic nature of Primordial War and generally deemphasize these sorts of &quot;Yozi apologism&quot; and ideas that Creation was built on cycles of usurpation which didn't fundamentally have any more or less moral legitimacy (the new gods triumphing over the old gods and so on). Tldr basically something fanbase just kind of stopped discussing too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T08:09:26-07:00","id":1404024,"title":"","content":"In 3E, Summon Elemental doesn't summon anything. It creates a magical servitor with an <i>extremely </i>minimal personality, a being that flatly cannot exist independently. Sometimes, the servitor will acquire sufficient personality and identity over the course of its service to continue existing, but otherwise, it's just a tool with a semblance of intellect and personality, morally equivalent to a character in a Sims game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T08:23:41-07:00","id":1404026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404024#post1404024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3E, Summon Elemental doesn't summon anything. It creates a magical servitor with an <i>extremely </i>minimal personality, a being that flatly cannot exist independently. Sometimes, the servitor will acquire sufficient personality and identity over the course of its service to continue existing, but otherwise, it's just a tool with a semblance of intellect and personality, morally equivalent to a character in a Sims game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but characters in the Sims game are not real. Creating a being with emotions, feelings, and a form of consciousness only to dismiss him when deemed useless stills feels kinda ... you know a bit immoral.<br /> <br /> I don't think there is a good definitive argument to say &quot;The moral implications are benign.&quot; But I think it's okay to play the game as if the moral implications were benign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T08:34:38-07:00","id":1404027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404022#post1404022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was loads of conversation about this during Exalted's original run. It got downgraded a little bit I think as change in conversation / previous devs looking to emphasise more the heroic nature of Primordial War and generally deemphasize these sorts of &quot;Yozi apologism&quot; and ideas that Creation was built on cycles of usurpation which didn't fundamentally have any more or less moral legitimacy (the new gods triumphing over the old gods and so on). Tldr basically something fanbase just kind of stopped discussing too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>One consideration that I think went into the original role of demons in Creation was that they wanted to go with a distinctly non-christian idea of demons, but the writers kept having to fight American readers' tendency to view demon-summoning as corrupting <i>because of demonic influence</i>, as opposed to it being corrupting <i>because it's slavery</i>. I think that part of the reason that the presentation shifted from &quot;demons obey&quot; to &quot;demons serve loyally, once bound&quot; was to break the assumption that the slavery was bad merely because of the slaves' motives, to force players to face the reality of what demon-binding means.<br /> <br /> Of course, this shift is a double-edged sword. Magically-enforced loyalty sounds a little easier to swallow than dealing with a slave that actively resents their orders. According to some philosophies, it might be better than the demon's &quot;natural&quot; lot in hell, though it violates their free will. (I think we had a thread on this a few months back, in fact.) But if it's easier to swallow, it's also easier to overlook as an evil endemic to the setting.<br /> <br /> Edit: Found the link: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ing-and-ethics</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 07-22-2020, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T08:39:01-07:00","id":1404028,"title":"","content":"I don't know up to what point it's relevant to the discussion here, but I think there are some interesting ideas for the moral discussion around the slavery (or humans and demons) in Exalted that I just happened to find. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2020/07/21/opinion/should-we-cancel-aristotle.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nytimes.com/2020/07/21/o...aristotle.html</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T08:44:53-07:00","id":1404029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404026#post1404026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but characters in the Sims game are not real. Creating a being with emotions, feelings, and a form of consciousness only to dismiss him when deemed useless stills feels kinda ... you know a bit immoral.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the end of the service, the sorceror does not &quot;dismiss&quot; the elemental. It flatly cannot endure beyond that term unless it's developed an actual personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T08:52:06-07:00","id":1404033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404029#post1404029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the service, the sorceror does not &quot;dismiss&quot; the elemental. It flatly cannot endure beyond that term unless it's developed an actual personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine if we could just create a pet for a day because we want company, and at the end of the day it &quot;disperses if it doesn't have a fully-formed personality&quot;. I'm not saying it's all black and white from a moral standpoint, but as I said, I don't think there is any satisfactory answer to conclude &quot;This is actually morally cool.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T08:57:50-07:00","id":1404036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404033#post1404033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine if we could just create a pet for a day because we want company, and at the end of the day it &quot;disperses if it doesn't have a fully-formed personality&quot;. I'm not saying it's all black and white from a moral standpoint, but as I said, I don't think there is any satisfactory answer to conclude &quot;This is actually morally cool.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine that you can create a pet with a normal lifespan of a day. If the pet develops enough, it can exceed that normal lifespan. Is it morally wrong to create something with a limited lifespan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T09:24:33-07:00","id":1404040,"title":"","content":"I see many points of contension here, some due to my analogy btw : If the elemental develops a personality, it means that at least for a time you enslaved a being with a fully formed personality. I also that it's at least morally grey to create a being with the potential of a conscious life for personal use with no other obligation (personal view), but I think it's not just personal given the many questions raised in bio-ethics concerning engineered life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T09:40:07-07:00","id":1404041,"title":"","content":"If you <i>are </i>keen on having demons around but aren't keen on the whole slave angle, you could just have an unbound demon as an ally or a retainer.<br /> <br /> You could be allied with a snarky bottle bug, a seductive Neomah and a blunt but loyal bloodape for 3 merit dots (bring kittens).<br /> <br /> There you go, now you are &quot;friends&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T10:21:04-07:00","id":1404044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404040#post1404040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see many points of contension here, some due to my analogy btw : If the elemental develops a personality, it means that at least for a time you enslaved a being with a fully formed personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see that. To quote from<i> Thus Spake Zarathustra</i>, &quot;What is the heaviest thing,&quot; asketh the load-bearing spirit, &quot;O ye heroes, that I may take it upon me and rejoice in my strength?&quot; Is it slavery to tell a person &quot;Do this!&quot; when &quot;Do this!&quot; is already that person's nature and desire? Remember always that a conjured elemental <i>is not human.</i> They are constructs, typically temporary, created to serve a purpose, and by their very nature have Defining Ties or Principles of loyalty to their creators or dedication to their task. I don't see how it's slavery to expect one to act in accordance with its nature. &quot;My hawk has become sapient! It is evil to make him aid me in the hunt!&quot;<br /> <br /> Hawk gives the sorceror a very level look. &quot;Um... right. So, when's the next hunt?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T13:20:13-07:00","id":1404078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~#post1403985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen anything yet about the PCs being slaver that enjoys from the fruit of their ancestor's conquests. I guess this isn't a story-hook that Exalted is interested in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Search &quot;Demon&quot;, Exalted board, topic titles only. There's also a couple of pages in Ask A Question.<br /> <br /> The most recent thread on this topic was mine:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e\"> By The Pricking of My Thumbs &ndash; John Doe&rsquo;s Guide to Demon Summoning (3E) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Introduction Recently I saw a post about someone struggling with summoned demons and thought there&rsquo;s scope for my to provide a mini-guide. I&rsquo;ve been playing </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics\"> On demon summoning and ethics - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Look, I know its probably done to death, and you all already thought of this... But has anyone thought of Demon-summoning? I mean, you are grabbing a creature, taking it from its home, and then binding it to your will to do whatever you want. From sex, to dying against an enemy, or labour. You're applying mind control to it to do stuff for you. Potentially forever. I mean, there's stuff about how life in Creation is a lot more nicer than Malfeas, but that sounds like a lot of the apologism for slavery. This applies for elementals as well. There's a lot of debate on the ethics of creating an A.I. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And as an added bonus, a thread about enslaving humans:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350831-dynast-abolitionist\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350831-dynast-abolitionist\"> Dynast Abolitionist - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350831-dynast-abolitionist\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350831-dynast-abolitionist </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So yeah, I kinda like this angle brought up in the other thread, and want to spin it off here! What sort of Dynast might go down the path of working to end slavery? Would that call to any particular profession, or be more a question of personal circumstances/belief? How would this affect how others view them? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T13:25:26-07:00","id":1404080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404044#post1404044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see that. To quote from<i> Thus Spake Zarathustra</i>, &quot;What is the heaviest thing,&quot; asketh the load-bearing spirit, &quot;O ye heroes, that I may take it upon me and rejoice in my strength?&quot; Is it slavery to tell a person &quot;Do this!&quot; when &quot;Do this!&quot; is already that person's nature and desire? Remember always that a conjured elemental <i>is not human.</i> They are constructs, typically temporary, created to serve a purpose, and by their very nature have Defining Ties or Principles of loyalty to their creators or dedication to their task. I don't see how it's slavery to expect one to act in accordance with its nature. &quot;My hawk has become sapient! It is evil to make him aid me in the hunt!&quot;<br /> <br /> Hawk gives the sorceror a very level look. &quot;Um... right. So, when's the next hunt?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with Neitzche (that's rather how my character sees things). But I'm far more comfortable agreeing with Rothbard:<br /> <br /> *Trigger Warning: Libertarian Ethics*<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">That the concept of a species ethic is part of the nature of the world may be seen, moreover, by contemplating the activities of other species in nature. It is more than a jest to point out that animals, after all, don't respect the &quot;rights&quot; of other animals; it is the condition of the world, and of all natural species, that they live by eating other species. Inter-species survival is a matter of tooth and claw. It would surely be absurd to say that the wolf is &quot;evil&quot; because he exists by devouring and &quot;aggressing against&quot; lambs, chickens, etc. The wolf is not an evil being who &quot;aggresses against&quot; other species; he is simply following the natural law of his own survival. Similarly for man. It is just as absurd to say that men &quot;aggress against&quot; cows and wolves as to say that wolves &quot;aggress against&quot; sheep. If, furthermore, a wolf attacks a man and the man kills him, it would be absurd to say either that the wolf was an &quot;evil aggressor&quot; or that the wolf was being &quot;punished&quot; for his &quot;crime.&quot; And yet such would be the implications of extending a natural-rights ethic to animals. Any concept of rights, of criminality, of aggression, can only apply to actions of one man or group of men against other human beings.<br /> <br /> What of the &quot;Martian&quot; problem? If we should ever discover and make contact with beings from other planets, could they be said to have the rights of human beings? It would depend on their nature. If our hypothetical &quot;Martians&quot; were like human beings \u2014 conscious, rational, able to communicate with us and participate in the division of labor \u2014 then presumably they too would possess the rights now confined to &quot;earthbound&quot; humans.<br /> <br /> But suppose, on the other hand, that the Martians also had the characteristics, the nature, of the legendary vampire, and could only exist by feeding on human blood. In that case, regardless of their intelligence, the Martians would be our deadly enemy and we could not consider that they were entitled to the rights of humanity. Deadly enemy, again, not because they were wicked aggressors, but because of the needs and requirements of their nature, which would clash ineluctably with ours.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Demons are an interesting case. It's not clear cut.<br /> <br /> But demons aren't humans.<br /> <br /> Summoned Elementals? I see how an internally consistent model of ethics can frame creating an Elemental as slavery. I don't see it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-22-2020, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T15:53:07-07:00","id":1404112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~#post1403985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People arguing endlessly about the morality of the Abyssal when they promise to kill the world in exchange for power[...]</div> </div> </div> </div> To be fair, that part was always pretty shallow bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T16:41:31-07:00","id":1404117,"title":"","content":"I think my CHARACTER would argue that the Yozi agreed to service to Creation as part of their surrender treaty, as reparation for their many atrocities upon Creation, and the Demons as extensions of the Yozi are merely fulfilling that promise as expressed in the power of binding.<br /> <br /> Of course this character wouldn\u2019t object to pow slavery, or self-sale old world slavery, either, while I obviously would. They do strongly object to mass chattel slavery.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile summoned elementals are more like familiars than slaves, at least initially. Those who do form their own sapient identity would indeed be entitled to the right of freedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-22-2020, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T18:25:43-07:00","id":1404144,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Summon Elemental does not actually \u201csummoning\u201d an elemental in Ex3 is the writer wanting to provide another way to get servants without all the slavery problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404112#post1404112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To be fair, that part was always pretty shallow bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I always thought \u201cAre they evil for X\u201d was supposedly one of the \u2018Seling-point\u201d of playing Abyssal, since they also have another one about soulsteel and Resonance too i.e \u201cAre they evil for using tortured souls as equipments/killing everybody as their nature\u201d. Though I guess it\u2019s possible for the whole Abyssal package to be shallow...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T19:17:49-07:00","id":1404156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404144#post1404144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I always thought \u201cAre they evil for X\u201d was supposedly one of the \u2018Seling-point\u201d of playing Abyssal, since they also have another one about soulsteel and Resonance too i.e \u201cAre they evil for using tortured souls as equipments/killing everybody as their nature\u201d. Though I guess it\u2019s possible for the whole Abyssal package to be shallow...</div> </div> </div> </div>More in 2E. In 1E you could sling a lot of epithets at the Abyssals, but \u201cevil\u201d wasn\u2019t really the aim. 1E seemed less... judgy, in my reading? Abyssals served a bunch of horrific old monsters, but, like, what superhuman military force didn\u2019t? They were death\u2019s tortured servants, not its masters. At least (one might say) you knew where you stood with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T19:37:30-07:00","id":1404158,"title":"","content":"Also, they're not promising to serve ancient powers that want to destroy their world <i>for power</i> - they're doing it <i>so they don't immediately die</i>. Remember, the offer's not even made to the prospective Abyssal until the very moment where they're staring death in the face.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you're going to condemn Abyssals for it, you might as well condemn everyone who survives in a capitalist society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T23:02:06-07:00","id":1404182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404158#post1404158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, they're not promising to serve ancient powers that want to destroy their world <i>for power</i> - they're doing it <i>so they don't immediately die</i>. Remember, the offer's not even made to the prospective Abyssal until the very moment where they're staring death in the face.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you're going to condemn Abyssals for it, you might as well condemn everyone who survives in a capitalist society.</div> </div> </div> </div>People in a capitalist society explicitly agree to actively murder folks?<br /> <br /> Trying to destroy the world so you don't die is equivalent to producing something people need to survive and freely trading for the things you need?<br /> <br /> Do you want to expand on that thought?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T23:49:27-07:00","id":1404188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404182#post1404182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People in a capitalist society explicitly agree to actively murder folks?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean yes.There's even multiple varieties of it with variable moral and legal values assigned to it based on perspective and which side of the philosophy you want to fall on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 07-23-2020, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T01:41:08-07:00","id":1404205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404182#post1404182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People in a capitalist society explicitly agree to actively murder folks?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're putting words in my mouth; I didn't say that.<br /> <br /> Agreeing to serve as an Abyssal does not necessitate that you ever directly murder someone (that's gonna depend on your Deathlord, of course, but it's not intrinsic to the condition of Abyssal-dom). \u200bBut you <i>are</i> agreeing to serve the interests of people who <i>know </i>their actions are sliding the entire world toward a series of crises that <i>will</i> result in mass deaths.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs an example, Seamstress of Dissolution from my seafaring game <b>never</b> directly killed another human. In fact, the only thing I recall her personally killing was one of the godly children of Siakal. She did, however, foster ancestor worship in the Neck and carry out a mission for the Silver Prince to help him recover the soul of a torpid Deathlord to prevent him from waking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-23-2020, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T06:24:26-07:00","id":1404233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404144#post1404144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Summon Elemental does not actually \u201csummoning\u201d an elemental in Ex3 is the writer wanting to provide another way to get servants without all the slavery problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC it was to solve the \u201cWhere <i>do</i> summoned elementals come from\u201d problem. That demon you just summoned from Hell wasn\u2019t doing anything you care about and starting in a year and two days you never have to see or think about it again, while in 2e you might have just pulled that elemental away from a nearby spirit court whose other members are now mad at you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T08:25:10-07:00","id":1404242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404205#post1404205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're putting words in my mouth; I didn't say that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your analogy doesn't make much sense, so trying to figure what you mean is inevitably going to lead to that. <br /> <br /> In no small part because people willing to be directly responsible for others' demise exist in whatever system or lack of it you can imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T06:26:57-07:00","id":1404389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404242#post1404242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your analogy doesn't make much sense, so trying to figure what you mean is inevitably going to lead to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t plan to contribute much to this aside except to say that I understood Alucard\u2019s point perfectly. He was comparing the Abyssal experience to life under capitalism, under which there\u2019s no way to survive that isn\u2019t inherently exploitive.<br /> <br /> The analogy makes sense as long as one doesn\u2019t take it super-literally, which is the case for all analogies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T07:29:09-07:00","id":1404398,"title":"","content":"Still doesn\u2019t make it a <i>good</i> analogy unless being just a couple steps away from looping around to the Neverborns\u2019 actual pitch (\u201cLife is suffering, Oblivion now\u201d) is the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T08:28:06-07:00","id":1404407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404158#post1404158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIf you're going to condemn Abyssals for it, you might as well condemn everyone who survives in a capitalist society.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this describes most of the world, both Creation an Earth, regardless of the economic system. Capitalist, communist, traditional pre-industrial trade systems. Unless you can confidently say that nobody in your massive market network is exploiting anyone else, you are in some way aiding that exploitation. Even in the smallest isolated communes people exploit eachother. You basically need to be a hermit to avoid it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T09:12:45-07:00","id":1404415,"title":"","content":"Well, no, there's a difference between humans exploiting one another and humans <i>supporting</i> one another. And just because people <i>have</i> exploited each other in societies doesn't mean we need to give up on society altogether and just become a race of hermits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T09:15:40-07:00","id":1404417,"title":"","content":"I think whereever we stand on moral judgements in respect to present day and past economic systems, objections to Abyssals tend to stand in nature of degree, not in kind. Doing what they do and agreeing to what they agree to do to survive. Not doing anything that consciously chooses to prioritize the self, to survive. So analogies that stray significantly in degree don't seem too useful and enlightening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T10:12:43-07:00","id":1404424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404415#post1404415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no, there's a difference between humans exploiting one another and humans <i>supporting</i> one another. And just because people <i>have</i> exploited each other in societies doesn't mean we need to give up on society altogether and just become a race of hermits.</div> </div> </div> </div>No we definitely don\u2019t need to give it up, but you\u2019re just not going to find one now, in history, or in the foreseeable future that doesn\u2019t exploit somebody somewhere. Your federal government does it, my federal government does it, we pay taxes, we\u2019re directly funding it. We\u2019re also directly finding welfare iniyiatives and meal programs that help feed people in crisis that have nowhere else to go, so it\u2019s not like it\u2019s all doom and gloom.<br /> <br /> Most Abyssals are much worse than that, but Creation in general is a pretty shitty place full of shitty people. You\u2019re kind of looking at the world of Dishonoured here. Most people suck, and the few people who don\u2019t really suck aren't in positions of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T10:27:06-07:00","id":1404426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404424#post1404424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Abyssals are much worse than that, but Creation in general is a pretty shitty place full of shitty people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get what you're driving at with this point; do you think I'm unaware that Creation is in a pretty bad place?<br /> <br /> \u200bMy point isn't that Abyssals aren't bad; it's just that <i>agreeing to be complicit in the destruction of the world because the alternative is a gun actively being pointed at your head</i> isn't even really a notable bullet point on the list..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T11:07:28-07:00","id":1404432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404426#post1404426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get what you're driving at with this point; do you think I'm unaware that Creation is in a pretty bad place?<br /> <br /> \u200bMy point isn't that Abyssals aren't bad; it's just that <i>agreeing to be complicit in the destruction of the world because the alternative is a gun actively being pointed at your head</i> isn't even really a notable bullet point on the list..</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s exactly my point? If somebody walks up to your Abyssal and says \u201cyou! You work for Thorns! Evil bastard!\u201d your Abyssal points to the Realm, Lookshy, Varangia, Whitewall, Rathess, Coral, Gem, etc and goes \u201cCompared to WHO exactly?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T13:16:06-07:00","id":1404445,"title":"","content":"I think this topic is a little off.<br /> <br /> Not that it's wrong, but rather that it's missing what Hatewheel tried to do in 3E: in 3E's supplemental material, aka Hatewheel's myriad forum posts he was making while throwing out the book for the third time, he argued very strenuously that demon summoning was immoral slavery. To him, that was natural, and I remember him getting into arguments with old forums regulars that, yes, Demon Summoning was immoral and to use it was to be an immoral person. This is rather continued to be brought forward by the text of summoning a demon, which says it is summoned screaming in rage, sorrow or fear, and that if you fail to bind it it will most likely be furious with you. The implication is, of course, demons are summoned unwillingly, and that, most likely, summoning a demon 'willingly' is something that, if it's at all possible, probably is something done a very different way.<br /> <br /> In some ways, to me, it felt like a response to 2E's 'build a bear workshop' demons. In 2E fandom, you could summon an infinite amount of demons that would infinitely craft you artifacts forever who only ever wanted to craft artifacts, because 2E was a wasteland of idiot ideas pushed to absurd limits by people whose only focus was winning a hypothetical game they'd never actually play. Hatewheel's strong stance about demon summoning being slavery felt like a backlash to the fandom idea, that it couldn't be moral or right, which would only make sense, because you're conscripting the losers of a war into forced slavery to labor for you. While it may not be out of sorts for some of the bronze age inspiration of Exalted, Exalted has always been willing to go 'just because it's what everyone is doing, doesn't mean it's right, and you should be willing to force your mortality onto the world if it upsets you', after all, even in ancient times like those- or more recent times-, you can always find people who stand up against the 'conventional' wisdom and do what is morally right (Mr. John Brown is a big, and constantly more and more relevant, example.).<br /> <br /> However, I think there's two distinct issues with this that 3E did not address, or addressed in such a way that is very ineffective. I'll do my best to discuss both of them:<br /> <br /> The first is the question of 'what if you actually want to learn from the Demons?' and 'How do you treat demons?'. Forced labor is wrong, that much is obvious; chattel slavery, sharecropping, kidnapping, all of that, I will take the assumption that everyone who reads this post understands that such things are naturally disgusting and doing them makes you a worse person. Not that people won't do them, but that there is an immorality to doing them. But the question that then comes up is, how do you engage with demons in a way that is not part of those institutions? Demons are trapped in a hellish world that is also innately hostile to non-demons, unless that has changed. You can go to the Demon World, but it is not simple, and it is not easy. This means interactions with them where you wish to treat with them as equals are difficult; if you wish to learn something from a demon, or to ask them to make something for you, there is little way to effectively do that. It's a forced separation that makes it almost impossible to really engage with demons outside of chattel slavery, which is a shame because, just like humans- which, again is probably entirely intentional-, demons are fascinating characters, each with their own idiosyncrasies and quirks, but that, like Gods, could have information that you as a player want to obtain, and if you wish to do this fairly or without engaging in violent practices, the ST sort of just has to make up a way for you to do this, or you're going to be involved in a multiple sessions long excursion to Malfeas which easily has the chance of totally dragging the game off track. I think if you really wanted to present Demon Summoning as a horrific way to interact with demons, there needs to be other ways to interact with them that don't involve that. Ways where you give up the safety of sorcerously binding something to your will to never harm you or to never stop doing the task you set to them to instead interact with the demons as thinking individuals with their own opinions you have to respect.<br /> <br /> The second is Summon Elemental. Summon Elemental seems to be an attempt to be a more 'moral' demon summoning. Rather then forcing something into slavery, you create a being that is specifically designed for the task, one without personality, drive, or history, that completes it's task then disappears. That is clearly the attempt to be more moral and 'correct' about summoning, because it's not inducting a living being into slavery. But even then, part of this is how it casually and completely misses the mark of offering an actual choice. If the intent is to present the idea that 'Demon summoning is easier, and more effective, but it's morally unjustifiable', Summon Elemental doesn't do this; there is no reason to learn Demon of the First Circle, which is where most sorcerers would tap out anyway, because Summon Elemental is effectively the exact same spell but without the baggage. There is no real choice within the first tier; you would always want Summon Elemental, even if you are, yourself, an amoral bastard who wants the easiest way, because a failed summoning of the Elemental doesn't result in it breaking free. It just fails and doesn't exist. This makes it infinitely safer for literally everyone with absolutely no trade-off, and it's also morally superior! Win-win! Which is kind of awkward.<br /> <br /> To clarify, I don't think this is wrong or even incorrect. I think it could be a very powerful statement on the uselessness and negativity of chattel slavery, of enslaving the defeated, of forced labor and dehumanization. I think that showing that those things aren't actually advantageous or beneficial, that they really just get the same result as being a good person, or maybe even a worse result, but that they're still continued because of greed or stagnation, are good. But I think that 3E doesn't show, that I've seen, that Demon Summoning only remains popular because of that stagnation. It seems to be relying, at least in part, on 2E's assumptions that Demon Summoning was 'more effective' to build a 3E belief that it's Demon Summoning is more effective, that can then be turned on it's head by going 'actually Elemental Summoning is just as good and it's not as morally reprehensible'. Which is where I think it fails. I think there should be some sort of attempt being made to present *why* this got popular in the first place. What made Demon Summoning popular, why does it continue to be popular when it's the much less efficient way to get supernatural helpers for a project. Chattel Slavery continued almost entirely because of racism where the elites used readings of cultural holy books to explain away why owning people as property was actually the will of their God. What cultural forces make Demon Summoning the popular form of bringing in magical labor? If the game can explain that, and offer ways to interact with Demons in ways that don't completely absorb the focus of the game into the area around demons, it would go a long way towards making the idea something that can be interacted with as more then a binary. Because if you don't have the first, then it comes across as a paper institution powered entirely by metagame conversations on the previous edition's forums, and if you don't have the second, you make it so that the only way to interact with a fascinating, nuanced group of characters is by engaging in either chattel slavery or forcing the ST, and the entire game, to bend to your desires, and that the best way to do anything with demons is to just leave them alone and never interact with them as the only moral choice, which is problematic in it's own way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T13:54:25-07:00","id":1404449,"title":"","content":"Demon of the First Circle is better supported.<br /> <br /> Summon Elemental might be more flexible in theory, but that means writing rules for your summon everyone can agree on, or using the, what? three? published Essence 1-3 Elementals?<br /> <br /> The demons are right there.<br /> <br /> (My character knows Demon of the First Circle.)<br /> <br /> And going to Malfeas is meant to be the moral option. Or taking the time to perform a Working. The quick and easy way is Summoning. The way that isn't the quick and easy way is neither quick nor easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-24-2020, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T15:25:46-07:00","id":1404464,"title":"","content":"Summon elemental brings life into existence to labor away from you. Life that starts as a blank slate but can grow into its own person\u2014and you can\u2019t stop it from growing necessarily. It\u2019s not more moral by default\u2014it\u2019s like making an AI to do a task or, perhaps less perfectly, its raising a kid for a job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T16:59:21-07:00","id":1404481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404464#post1404464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Summon elemental brings life into existence to labor away from you. Life that starts as a blank slate but can grow into its own person\u2014and you can\u2019t stop it from growing necessarily. It\u2019s not more moral by default\u2014it\u2019s like making an AI to do a task or, perhaps less perfectly, its raising a kid for a job.</div> </div> </div> </div>certainly the case, in theory, but if the Elemental does become more then a laborer, then when the contract ends it becomes real when the contract ends, which again sidesteps the moral issue to me; if your elemental does become real and a fleshed out individual, then all you've really done is brought life into the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T17:56:34-07:00","id":1404491,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, there\u2019s a seemingly substantial portion of the fandom that firmly believes that to create anything with any degree of intellect or personality or the potential for such is fundamentally immoral if the creation\u2019s actions after its creation are constrained in any way. I\u2019ve never understood that; it\u2019s exactly saying that creating a computer system with learning capability is immoral. Which leads logically to the conclusion that search engines are immoral to create, any program with auto-complete is immoral to use, it\u2019s morally wrong to play a game with adaptive difficulty or use \u201cyou might like\u201d feature. The problems with this view go much further, but taking the position to its illogical extreme would serve only to anger everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T18:22:51-07:00","id":1404494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~#post1403985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People arguing endlessly about the morality of the Abyssal when they promise to kill the world in exchange for power, but I haven't seen anything yet about the PCs being slaver that enjoys from the fruit of their ancestor's conquests. I guess this isn't a story-hook that Exalted is interested in?</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason we don't talk about demon-summoning all the time is because it leads to total philosophy-slogs like this conversation is inexorably becoming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T20:25:00-07:00","id":1404512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404494#post1404494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason we don't talk about demon-summoning all the time is because it leads to total philosophy-slogs like this conversation is inexorably becoming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bouncing ideas off other people is pretty good I think (also help that I have never seen the old <i>old</i> forum so this is new for me).<br /> <br /> Plus I have a bunch of For/Against examples when discussing demon=slavery IC now, I definitely never think that \u201cThey aren\u2019t human so no <i>human</i> rights for them\u201d would be a real point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T21:43:53-07:00","id":1404522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404494#post1404494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason we don't talk about demon-summoning all the time is because it leads to total philosophy-slogs like this conversation is inexorably becoming.</div> </div> </div> </div>That or it ends right away with several &quot;Yes it's pretty clearly slavery, and?&quot;s in a row.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T00:54:32-07:00","id":1404540,"title":"","content":"The problem with condemning Abyssals for choosing to accept Abyssal Exaltation at the moment of death is that if they refuse, no actual good is accomplished. They just die and the Deathlord only suffers the moderate inconvenience of having to find another candidate. You can argue about the personal taint of moral corruption, but you can also say &quot;Well, I should say yes because the next person the insane superghost picks might be worse than me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also yes of course demon summoning is immoral slavery. That angle on Exalted is not super interested in keeping your hand away from the atrocity button.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T01:57:29-07:00","id":1404550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404540#post1404540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with condemning Abyssals for choosing to accept Abyssal Exaltation at the moment of death is that if they refuse, no actual good is accomplished. They just die and the Deathlord only suffers the moderate inconvenience of having to find another candidate.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if that candidate does the right thing and agrees not to kill the world, and the next and the next, the Deathlord is stymied.<br /> <br /> &quot;If I don't murder my children, they'll only die of something else.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can argue about the personal taint of moral corruption, but you can also say &quot;Well, I should say yes because the next person the insane superghost picks might be worse than me.&quot; </div> </div> </div>&quot;If I don't murder my children humanely in their sleep, a maniac might set them on fire.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or the next person might also refuse. Or be better than you.<br /> <br /> You're not responsible for what other people <i>might</i> do, you're responsible for what you <b>do</b> do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404540#post1404540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also yes of course demon summoning is immoral slavery. That angle on Exalted is not super interested in keeping your hand away from the atrocity button.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think The Unconquered Sun agrees with you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T04:56:30-07:00","id":1404569,"title":"","content":"Honestly with the Abyssals, I guess I would perhaps deemphasize the arguments around them as good people who have morally compromised themselves by taking conscious choice and fully informed choice to doom the world and who are very troubled by this and so on.<br /> <br /> You might get more out of positioning them as people who accept the power and survival for the immediate chance to protect the communities they served in life, take revenge, plan to throw themselves into almost suicidal struggles against the very forces that give them power, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T05:41:30-07:00","id":1404573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404156#post1404156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More in 2E. In 1E you could sling a lot of epithets at the Abyssals, but \u201cevil\u201d wasn\u2019t really the aim. 1E seemed less... judgy, in my reading? Abyssals served a bunch of horrific old monsters, but, like, what superhuman military force didn\u2019t? They were death\u2019s tortured servants, not its masters. At least (one might say) you knew where you stood with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I used to hang out with a few first edition players who felt like Neph basically turned on them in 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T06:53:18-07:00","id":1404583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404550#post1404550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if that candidate does the right thing and agrees not to kill the world, and the next and the next, the Deathlord is stymied.<br /> <br /> &quot;If I don't murder my children, they'll only die of something else.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A) That quote isn\u2019t comparable to the point you\u2019re responding to, because there are a lot of steps between \u201caccept deathly power\u201d and \u201cworld ends.\u201d<br /> B) Most Deathlords probably aren\u2019t that direct about the Neverborn\u2019s ultimate aims when approaching candidates. Unless they\u2019ve found a candidate that\u2019s open to ending the world, which is possible.<br /> C) Even if the Deathlord is super-direct, it\u2019s possible to enter into the deal with the intention of betraying them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're not responsible for what other people <i>might</i> do, you're responsible for what you <b>do</b> do. </div> </div> </div>This is a matter of opinion and/or philosophical debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 07-25-2020, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T07:18:16-07:00","id":1404586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404583#post1404583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Deathlords probably aren\u2019t that direct about the Neverborn\u2019s ultimate aims when approaching candidates. Unless they\u2019ve found a candidate that\u2019s open to ending the world, which is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed; the closest I've ever come to being informed of a mission to destroy the world in a scene of Abyssal Exaltation is when my Dusk, Son-of-Void Dragon, was told he would be given a chance to take vengeance on his betrayers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T10:02:53-07:00","id":1404597,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I think takes on the Abyssal Exaltation where the Deathlord always tells the potential Abyssal Exalt &quot;If you take this, you're agreeing to kill the world,&quot; like it somehow doesn't work if the Deathlord doesn't do full disclosure and therefore all Abyssals <b>definitely are</b> making an informed choice to kill the world when they accept the Exaltation, regardless of whether they plan to go back on their word later, are fucking dumb. I assume most Abyssals accepting the Black Exaltation don't get told shit (beyond &quot;Hey you're dying do you want to not die and also get a bunch of power in exchange for pledging loyalty to me, a skeleton in a robe with a scythe?&quot;). If something contradicting that got written into Abyssals 2e to make them less ambiguous, I don't care.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404550#post1404550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think The Unconquered Sun agrees with you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. The Unconquered Sun thinks that if demons didn't want to get used as slave labor forever they shouldn't have gotten themselves sent to jail by serving in the wrong army and/or having the wrong parents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 07-25-2020, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T10:37:27-07:00","id":1404600,"title":"","content":"I guess broadly speaking I don't think the greater cosmological, metaphysical, or political powers of Creation subscribe to philosophies of introspection, informed consent, or a commitment to moral integrity defined by rigorous self-criticism in the name of consistency no matter how uncomfortable it is, though I <i>absolutely do</i> think the audience should <i>examine</i> Creation through those lenses.<br /> <br /> Creation is the sort of place where most of the people in power, all the way up to the highest god, think that authority confers the right to maintain that authority through violence applied to those who'd defy it, and that things like &quot;Mercy&quot; and &quot;Full disclosure&quot; are, in the words of Kid Spock in the J.J. Abrams Star Trek reboot, &quot;Morally praiseworthy but not morally obligatory.&quot; Which means that if you're someone's boss, let's say because their great-great-grandfather promised you fealty in exchange for being spared execution after you beat them in a war, or because you tricked them into saying they agree you're their boss, and this person whose boss you are decides they don't want you to be their boss anymore and absolutely will not let you boss them around anymore even to the point of you beating them to death, then showing mercy in the face of their defiance by stopping short of beating them to death probably makes you a good person, but <i>not</i> stopping short of beating them to death <i>doesn't</i> make you a <i>bad</i> person. Because you're the boss; what were you supposed to do, accept their theft of your authority without standing your ground?<br /> <br /> And this informs everything from &quot;Do Deathlords tell their Abyssals what the Black Exaltation entails?&quot; to &quot;How okay do people in the setting think it is to use demon slave labor?&quot;<br /> <br /> Shit's fucked. For the purposes of the genre that Exalted occupies, shit is supposed to be fucked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T10:40:09-07:00","id":1404601,"title":"","content":"I also have another essay about the difference between moral systems that draw a categorical line between non-sexual and sexual violence and coercion and those that don't, but I don't know how dark I want to get here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 07-25-2020, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T11:23:47-07:00","id":1404605,"title":"","content":"I'm sure I'll catch up on this thread at some point, but for now...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404597#post1404597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I think takes on the Abyssal Exaltation where the Deathlord always tells the potential Abyssal Exalt &quot;If you take this, you're agreeing to kill the world,&quot; like it somehow doesn't work if the Deathlord doesn't do full disclosure and therefore all Abyssals <b>definitely are</b> making an informed choice to kill the world when they accept the Exaltation, regardless of whether they plan to go back on their word later, are fucking dumb. I assume most Abyssals accepting the Black Exaltation don't get told shit (beyond &quot;Hey you're dying do you want to not die and also get a bunch of power in exchange for pledging loyalty to me, a skeleton in a robe with a scythe?&quot;). If something contradicting that got written into Abyssals 2e to make them less ambiguous, I don't care.</div> </div> </div> </div>For my part, I would like something to that effect because I like the idea of Abyssal Exaltation having a bit of ceremony to it. I kind of want that to be a recurring element of being Abyssal Exalted overall.<br /> <br /> Complementary to that, I would like the idea for what Abyssals do with regards to a slowly dying world to have range beyond &quot;gather an army and weapons and go around just directly slaughtering people&quot;; that it extends into areas more uncanny and mystical, a deepening melancholy for the world. That there are Abyssals who are tormented by their engagement with this, but in the manner of a Gothic antihero rather than somebody trying to sneak away from a force that would demand they mass murder. The Essence of Abyssals being less about killing and more about giving up on life and/or finding the embrace of death more compelling.<br /> <br /> As time goes by, I become concerned that the Chivalry of Death will be a concept quietly dropped from them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T11:38:48-07:00","id":1404608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404600#post1404600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Creation is the sort of place where most of the people in power, all the way up to the highest god, think that authority confers the right to maintain that authority through violence applied to those who'd defy it, and that things like &quot;Mercy&quot; and &quot;Full disclosure&quot; are, in the words of Kid Spock in the J.J. Abrams Star Trek reboot, &quot;Morally praiseworthy but not morally obligatory.&quot; Which means that if you're someone's boss, let's say because their great-great-grandfather promised you fealty in exchange for being spared execution after you beat them in a war, or because you tricked them into saying they agree you're their boss, and this person whose boss you are decides they don't want you to be their boss anymore and absolutely will not let you boss them around anymore even to the point of you beating them to death, then showing mercy in the face of their defiance by stopping short of beating them to death probably makes you a good person, but <i>not</i> stopping short of beating them to death <i>doesn't</i> make you a <i>bad</i> person. Because you're the boss; what were you supposed to do, accept their theft of your authority without standing your ground?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a tad concerned that this is overly focused on the introspection of the people with power without regards to the outlook of people beneath them.<br /> <br /> I mean, I guess it matters for how one approaches and characterises those figures who employ power in such a manner to not totally write them off, but that it bears considering that other people will still observe and pass judgement on them.<br /> <br /> My mind goes to Roman politics at the end of the Republican era. Caesar has popularity with the people when he has things like the victories of an upstanding Roman and disseminates war booty among the populace, but they still raise eyebrows when he's doing things like commemorating victory in battle against other Romans, on the verge of executing a teenage princess from a highly prestigious lineage, and pretty openly having an extramarital affair with a foreign queen with alien customs and putting a statue of her in his family shrine. Caesar's lieutenant ceremonially offers him a crown, and some accounts suggest that this actually is intended as the pretext for assuming kingship but for the fact that the crowds respond pretty angrily to the spectacle. But conversely, when Caesar is ganged up on and stabbed in the Senate hall, his popularity helps bolster up the public opinion that such a thing is dreadfully done despite the assassins' arguments that the action was both moral and legal, and the riot at Caesar's funeral sends those conspirators to flight.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm saying is that a discussion such as this should not exclude the input of society at large, and that we do indeed get historical precedent for society at large indeed condemning the unmerciful liege in a manner that creates further difficulties.<br /> <br /> I think that Exalted already has enough problems with people enthusiastically pursuing the angle of &quot;the power of these individuals means that they can effectively tell society at large to go fuck themselves, Idowatiwan&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T11:44:57-07:00","id":1404612,"title":"","content":"Okay, that, too. &quot;What do peasants think is good?&quot; is a different question than &quot;What does the king think is good?&quot; <i>The Moral Economy of the Peasant</i> is an important source.<br /> <br /> But I was asked what the UCS thinks about demon summoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T12:55:05-07:00","id":1404619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404550#post1404550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if that candidate does the right thing and agrees not to kill the world, and the next and the next, the Deathlord is stymied.<br /> <br /> &quot;If I don't murder my children, they'll only die of something else.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but if is <i>if</i>.<br /> <br /> You can easily perform any number of substitutions to make this isomorphic with real-world evils, where if the [person in situation X] does the right thing and [stands up to entity Y], then [entity Y] is stymied. And yet we still have corruption and tyranny, not a world where yet another whistleblower or a labor organizer or a revolutionary <i>inevitably</i> stands up after everyone before them is broken on the wheel of power, stymieing those in power indefinitely.<br /> <br /> (That said, Lea's proposals have a lot of merit to them, and are under discussion by the dev team.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T14:35:02-07:00","id":1404642,"title":"","content":"I like SLS' proposals, because I vaguely remember Neph at some point late 2E basically saying 'an Infernal can be lied to about what taking an Infernal Exaltation means, so they can be morally innocent to what they're doing, but a Deathlord can not lie when offering the Abyssal Exaltation, and every person who agrees with it is accepting their job is to destroy the world'. I think that really is kind of a dumb thing to do for exactly the same philosophical reasons that this thread is sort of getting into, which makes it uninteresting.<br /> <br /> Which I think goes into what Lioness and others have been talking about with the idea that he 'turned' on Abyssals in 2E, though I wasn't here from 1E or even early 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T15:11:58-07:00","id":1404649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404597#post1404597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah. The Unconquered Sun thinks that if demons didn't want to get used as slave labor forever they shouldn't have gotten themselves sent to jail by serving in the wrong army and/or having the wrong parents.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404600#post1404600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess broadly speaking I don't think the greater cosmological, metaphysical, or political powers of Creation subscribe to philosophies of introspection, informed consent, or a commitment to moral integrity defined by rigorous self-criticism in the name of consistency no matter how uncomfortable it is, though I <i>absolutely do</i> think the audience should <i>examine</i> Creation through those lenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I absolutely, totally, and in every way disagree.<br /> <br /> The setting has to be examined within the confines of the setting. It's the Paladin Problem: if D&amp;Ds Pelor says &quot;killing murderers is Lawful Good&quot;, then within the context of the game killing murderers is Lawful Good. Dragging real life arguments about capital punishment to your game table in the hopes of getting +1 to Hit isn't apropos.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, if you wanted to critic Exalted as a media and wanted to apply a moral objectivist set of standards, I have no beef with that. But just as, objectively, one can't ride a horse into the sky because of the laws of physics, Exalted's laws of ethics are different to ours.<br /> <br /> Using demon summoning to safely explore themes around oppression is fertile storytelling ground. But... well unless a Dev is going to chime in and say &quot;The Unconquered Sun is now objectively immoral&quot;, then the immorality of demon summoning remains less than self-evident, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404619#post1404619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but if is <i>if</i>.<br /> <br /> You can easily perform any number of substitutions to make this isomorphic with real-world evils, where if the [person in situation X] does the right thing and [stands up to entity Y], then [entity Y] is stymied. And yet we still have corruption and tyranny, not a world where yet another whistleblower or a labor organizer or a revolutionary <i>inevitably</i> stands up after everyone before them is broken on the wheel of power, stymieing those in power indefinitely.<br /> <br /> (That said, Lea's proposals have a lot of merit to them, and are under discussion by the dev team.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure but don't you <i>want</i> &quot;another whistleblower or a labor organizer or a revolutionary&quot; to stand up and stop this evil? Isn't stopping the evil <i>better</i> than just <i>allowing</i> &quot;corruption and tyranny&quot;?<br /> <br /> If someone keeps their head down, looks the other way, does nothing... we can all understand and relate to that. But that doesn't mean it's the right thing to do.<br /> <br /> Being complicit in tyranny and corruption is the wrong thing to do. And I don't think any of you really need me to tell you that.<br /> <br /> If a trans person is getting beaten up, and your options are pledge alligence to the Neo Nazi gang doing the beating and go about your business, or come to that trans person's aid, then there's a right thing to do and a wrong thing. There's a million reasons why someone would choose the wrong thing, but they're choosing the wrong thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T15:43:57-07:00","id":1404659,"title":"","content":"From my perspective, I wouldn't be totally against some element of a &quot;Collaborator's Dilemma&quot; in the Abyssal Exalted. *But*, I would hope that Exalted approaches this as critically and skeptically as it does all other narratives that tend to justify folks who seize power and take questionable actions, justified to themselves and others that this is in order that power does not fall to a worse and less just holder.<br /> <br /> There's a bit of subtextual skepticism towards &quot;Heavy is the head that wears the crown&quot; - or at least that's something Stephen persuaded me, among other readers of his posts, in the past! - as being mostly or often self-serving rhetoric and it would be a shame, or at least philosophically inconsistent, not to extend that same critical eye here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T16:06:51-07:00","id":1404662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404649#post1404649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The setting has to be examined within the confines of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div> And within the confines of the setting, demon summoning is slavery.<br /> <br /> Your characters don't have to agree, or even care (I say they shouldn't), but if you don't want to play a slaver, don't play a demon summoner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T16:56:36-07:00","id":1404672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404659#post1404659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my perspective, I wouldn't be totally against some element of a &quot;Collaborator's Dilemma&quot; in the Abyssal Exalted. *But*, I would hope that Exalted approaches this as critically and skeptically as it does all other narratives that tend to justify folks who seize power and take questionable actions, justified to themselves and others that this is in order that power does not fall to a worse and less just holder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, though, the Abyssals are not, in that moment, nakedly seizing power. They are seizing <i>their continued existence</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou can judge Abyssals all you want, but do it once they pop the top off someone else's skull like a bottle cap and drink from it, or forge someone's soul into a boomerang; rather than condemn them for <i>deciding to live</i> in a shitty world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-25-2020, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T17:02:35-07:00","id":1404673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404662#post1404662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And within the confines of the setting, demon summoning is slavery.<br /> <br /> Your characters don't have to agree, or even care (I say they shouldn't), but if you don't want to play a slaver, don't play a demon summoner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but usually slavery is connoted as a bad thing. In Exalted it's much less clear if it's good or bad. (Which I think is a good thing)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T17:10:33-07:00","id":1404675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404649#post1404649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The setting has to be examined within the confines of the setting. It's the Paladin Problem: if D&amp;Ds Pelor says &quot;killing murderers is Lawful Good&quot;, then within the context of the game killing murderers is Lawful Good.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, Pelor is neither the supreme god of D&amp;D, nor is he even Lawful Good (he's Neutral Good, or just Good in 4e). Nor do the gods in D&amp;D even define alignments.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being complicit in tyranny and corruption is the wrong thing to do. And I don't think any of you really need me to tell you that. </div> </div> </div>And yet you sure seem to have chosen to continue living.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a trans person is getting beaten up, and your options are pledge alligence to the Neo Nazi gang doing the beating and go about your business, or come to that trans person's aid, then there's a right thing to do and a wrong thing. There's a million reasons why someone would choose the wrong thing, but they're choosing the wrong thing. </div> </div> </div>Wow, a false dichotomy <i>and</i> Godwin's Law.<br /> <br /> \u200bObviously you have more options than <i>just</i> &quot;help the trans person&quot; or &quot;pledge allegiance to Nazis.&quot; And you won't be able to do <i>any</i> of them <b>if you're dead.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-25-2020, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T17:14:38-07:00","id":1404676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404675#post1404675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, Pelor is neither the supreme god of D&amp;D, nor is he even Lawful Good (he's Neutral Good, or just Good in 4e). Nor do the gods in D&amp;D even define alignments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lawful Good divinities usually advise the same thing, and they are Lawful Good. They don't define alignments, but they belong to their alignment, and are usually recognized by the metaphysic of the DD universe by gaining powers and planes over the chosen alignment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T17:20:38-07:00","id":1404677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404676#post1404676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lawful Good divinities<b> usually advise the same thing</b>, and they are Lawful Good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they don't. One of the intrinsic properties of goodness is a respect for life; likewise the lawful alignment aligns itself with order and justice. Murder is against both of those things, so even if Saint Cuthbert <i>wants you to</i> break into the Asmodeus cultist mayor's manor and stove in his head while he's sleeping, that won't make it Lawful Good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T17:30:30-07:00","id":1404680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404649#post1404649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... well unless a Dev is going to chime in and say &quot;The Unconquered Sun is now objectively immoral&quot;, then the immorality of demon summoning remains less than self-evident, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a dev, I am going to chime in and say that &quot;objectively immoral&quot; is a meaningless expression in terms of Exalted-the-published-setting. The game explicitly and overtly rejects objective morality. Players may bring their views of objective morality to the table; they may construct characters who believe in one form or another of objective morality; these things are desirable! The setting will also attempt to present the harms done by people and institutions in a clear and unobstructed way, to avoid apologia for such harm in the real world. Much of the interest of Exalted play comes from the clash of ideologies that comes forward when PCs have the power to impose their ideologies on the world around them. But the game is not going to decide for you what's right and what's wrong, nor how to resolve moral complexities and ethical dilemmas.<br /> <br /> So, no, I am not going to say as a dev that the Unconquered Sun is objectively moral or objectively immoral.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404649#post1404649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure but don't you <i>want</i> &quot;another whistleblower or a labor organizer or a revolutionary&quot; to stand up and stop this evil? Isn't stopping the evil <i>better</i> than just <i>allowing</i> &quot;corruption and tyranny&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kant's categorical imperative is all very well as a personal ethical lodestar, but it is fallacious to assume that <i>desiring</i> that your moral stance would be a universal law means that it <i>is</i> a universal law. You argue that if everyone says no to the Deathlords' bargain, then the Deathlord will be forever stymied; but desiring for that to be the case will not make it so, because the people of Creation are written to be like people in the real world. People in the real world make all manner of selfish and destructive bargains for any number of reasons less dire than &quot;or else you unavoidably die this very moment.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404649#post1404649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a trans person is getting beaten up, and your options are pledge alligence to the Neo Nazi gang doing the beating and go about your business, or come to that trans person's aid, then there's a right thing to do and a wrong thing. There's a million reasons why someone would choose the wrong thing, but they're choosing the wrong thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This metaphor maps poorly to the thing it purports to refer, and does so in an emotionally manipulative way. Please don't do that. Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T17:34:55-07:00","id":1404681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404673#post1404673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but usually slavery is connoted as a bad thing. In Exalted it's much less clear if it's good or bad. (Which I think is a good thing)</div> </div> </div> </div> The game is pretty clear on what slavery does to people, just as it doesn't really equivocate on imperialism.<br /> <br /> It's just that the game doesn't bar us from playing &quot;good guys&quot; just because they happen to be wrong about these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T18:39:47-07:00","id":1404685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404642#post1404642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I think goes into what Lioness and others have been talking about with the idea that he 'turned' on Abyssals in 2E, though I wasn't here from 1E or even early 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, I don't know all the minutiae of why they felt betrayed. <br /> <br /> It could be the 1st to 2nd edition Abyssal equivalent of &quot;I don't want my Infernals to be decadent, I want them to be Rockstars from Hell!&quot; I mean I doubt it, but fans having weird takes on source material is always going to be a thing. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T19:17:31-07:00","id":1404691,"title":"","content":"First edition Abyssals were really popular, you guys. <i>So popular.</i> It's hard to believe now, but they were like tied with Dragon-Blooded for #2 most popular Exalt type after Solars. They were basically goth Solars and you could easily run them as goth Solars, only instead of Limit Break they got to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bIqpp3_fTnc\" target=\"_blank\">play out the Vampire Hunter D Bloodlust intro with the environment responding to their presence</a>. <i>Instead of</i> Limit Break, not in addition to it! Like, do you want to play a Solar, except your sword is Stormbringer from Elric, your outfit is all black and red, and sometimes when you walk into a room everyone else in the room starts weeping blood?<br /> <br /> Neph thought this was fuckin' dumb and they should cater to a more focused experience and not be tailor made for people who wanted Solars, But 20% Cooler.<i>Also</i>, he was suffering from really bad untreated depression and had gotten into the habit of turning his manuscripts in so late that Geoff didn't have time to make changes to them in development, and he'd decided this meant that his work was so good it could always be used as-is.<br /> <br /> So. Abyssals 2e went from cooler goth Solars to a meditation on evil designed to dis-incentivize easy fun, filtered through both a) the sort of absolutist lack of self-forgiveness and rejection of nuance that can come from clinical depression and b) total confidence on the part of the writer in the quality of his ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 07-25-2020, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T20:03:09-07:00","id":1404694,"title":"","content":"It seems to me like we should distinguish a couple different questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Is it morally right to stand up to the Deathlords?<br /> 2. Is almost everyone selected to be an Abyssal going to stand up to the Deathlords?<br /> 3. What is the most effective way to stand up to the Deathlords, if you are selected to be an Abyssal?<br /> <br /> 1 and 2 are not very interesting questions.<br /> <br /> As Eric pointed out, the Exalted setting does not contain an objective morality, but in the point of view of most people who played the game and most humans within Creation, the answer to question 1 is yes. <br /> <br /> The answer to question 2 is pretty clearly no. It's possible that a majority might stand up, but probably not even that, especially if the Deathlords show some skill in selecting their targets.<br /> <br /> I think question 3 is the only one that people here are interested in debating.<br /> <br /> One proposal is to refuse the Abyssal Exaltation and die. Another would be to accept, serve the Deathlord, and try to do as little damage as possible. A third would be to accept, flee the Deathlord's service as soon as possible, and then run as far away as possible. <br /> <br /> It obviously depends on how exactly Abyssals and Deathlords are described in this edition, but the third option seems by far the most effective to me. You deprive the Deathlord of a useful servant for as long as you survive, which if they find you and kill you might not be very long (but still probably more time than it takes to find a willing servant) but if you avoid their reach, might be decades, centuries, or, effectively, forever.<br /> <br /> As long as escape is possible (and I understand from an unrelated source that even in 2e it was) the choice to accept or reject Abyssal Exaltation can't be seen exactly as a choice to collaborate with oppression or reject it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T20:08:03-07:00","id":1404695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404649#post1404649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure but don't you <i>want</i> &quot;another whistleblower or a labor organizer or a revolutionary&quot; to stand up and stop this evil? Isn't stopping the evil <i>better</i> than just <i>allowing</i> &quot;corruption and tyranny&quot;?<br /> <br /> If someone keeps their head down, looks the other way, does nothing... we can all understand and relate to that. But that doesn't mean it's the right thing to do.<br /> <br /> Being complicit in tyranny and corruption is the wrong thing to do. And I don't think any of you really need me to tell you that.<br /> <br /> If a trans person is getting beaten up, and your options are pledge alligence to the Neo Nazi gang doing the beating and go about your business, or come to that trans person's aid, then there's a right thing to do and a wrong thing. There's a million reasons why someone would choose the wrong thing, but they're choosing the wrong thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other people have pointed out how this comparison is off the rails compared to what we were talking about. More broadly, I think it might be worth considering that something about this conversation has struck a nerve to the point that you're not responding in a measured way to the things other people are saying. I don't think you're the only one getting there, and I'm certainly in no position to tell you (or anyone else here) what to do, but maybe consider taking a break? I think I might do so as well. The thread will be here when we get back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T20:19:59-07:00","id":1404698,"title":"","content":"The &quot;If I said no, I'd have been killed and they would just have had someone else do it&quot; argument is an excuse a lot of people involved in the Holocaust made. At some point that isn't good enough, the answer is, &quot;The fact that you didn't choose to die over doing <i>that</i> is exactly why you're a monster.&quot;<br /> <br /> The key question is, then, is, what is the &quot;it&quot; that you are doing when you accept the Abyssal Exaltation?<br /> <br /> Well, in 1e, there was some ambiguity. A candidate would only get the Exaltation if he'd &quot;accept that death must inevitably come to all things, that in death all things arrive at last at their holy, predestined, final peace&quot; and then accept &quot;the opportunity to help purify the world, to deliver the living to their final ends and to foment the worship of death in all Creation.&quot; (Abyssals, p.108).<br /> <br /> In 2e, it was &quot;To receive the Black Exaltation, the mortal must vow to serve the goals of the dead yet undying Neverborn. That is, she must devote her newly given power to the cause of plunging Creation into the Underworld and the Underworld ultimately into the Abyss.&quot; (MOEP:Abyssals p.29).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T20:43:40-07:00","id":1404700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404649#post1404649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The setting has to be examined within the confines of the setting. It's the Paladin Problem: if D&amp;Ds Pelor says &quot;killing murderers is Lawful Good&quot;, then within the context of the game killing murderers is Lawful Good. Dragging real life arguments about capital punishment to your game table in the hopes of getting +1 to Hit isn't apropos.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Except even in the D&amp;D-verse, there are other Good Gods, including <i><b>The</b></i> God of Good and <i><b>The</b></i> God of Law, who would answer your premise with a resounding &quot;NO&quot;, therefore giving the characters the opportunity for conflict<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T20:56:47-07:00","id":1404703,"title":"","content":"WIth regards to the other topic, my understanding is that summoning is not necessarily worse for demons than imprisonment in Malfeas is normally. Of course this isn't an ethical justification for slavery, but rather a criticism of Malfeas.<br /> <br /> Luckily, if your character comes to the same conclusion about ethics, the core book has a solution for you!<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Invite </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">an unbound First Circle demon into Creation in a ritual that culminates at midnight.&quot; is a Terrestrial Ambition 1 Working. The same for a Second Circle demon is Celestial Ambition 2 Working, which must (usually) culminate on the night of the full moon. <br /> <br /> Even a lowly mortal sorcerer can, if they disagree with the way the Incarnae and their Exalted servants have arranged Creation, work to liberate the imprisoned souls of Malfeas, 2 xp at a time.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T22:16:14-07:00","id":1404705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404698#post1404698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;If I said no, I'd have been killed and they would just have had someone else do it&quot; argument is an excuse a lot of people involved in the Holocaust made. At some point that isn't good enough, the answer is, &quot;The fact that you didn't choose to die over doing <i>that</i> is exactly why you're a monster.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Abyssals are genocidal monsters but try not to compare them to Nazis.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T23:26:59-07:00","id":1404713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404698#post1404698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in 1e, there was some ambiguity. A candidate would only get the Exaltation if he'd &quot;accept that death must inevitably come to all things, that in death all things arrive at last at their holy, predestined, final peace&quot; and then accept &quot;the opportunity to help purify the world, to deliver the living to their final ends and to foment the worship of death in all Creation.&quot; (Abyssals, p.108).</div> </div> </div> </div>And, you'll note, that even in 1e an Abyssal could then try and weasel out of that decision. While redemption wasn't given mechanics until 2e, an Abyssal ultimately possesses free will, meaning that an Abyssal who accepts the Mask of Winters' offer, learns his plans, and then defects and tells a circle of Solars what he learned from the Deathlord will have tangibly done <i>vastly more good</i> than the <i>prospective</i> Abyssal who told the Black Exaltation to go fuck itself when the Maiden of Endings came a-knocking.<br /> <br /> \u200bHeck, he's even depriving the Mask of an Abyssal <i>to the same extent</i> as the so-called &quot;moral&quot; refuser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-26-2020, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T00:37:22-07:00","id":1404721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404672#post1404672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, though, the Abyssals are not, in that moment, nakedly seizing power. They are seizing <i>their continued existence</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou can judge Abyssals all you want, but do it once they pop the top off someone else's skull like a bottle cap and drink from it, or forge someone's soul into a boomerang; rather than condemn them for <i>deciding to live</i> in a shitty world.</div> </div> </div> </div>lol, I agree with this very obvious point, and think it's a shame I deleted a codacil to my post making it clear that this was the case (&quot;This is unnecessary and obvious! People will get it without that.&quot; I thought).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T00:49:00-07:00","id":1404724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404713#post1404713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bHeck, he's even depriving the Mask of an Abyssal <i>to the same extent</i> as the so-called &amp;quot;moral&amp;quot; refuser.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until you consider Resonance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404680#post1404680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a dev, I am going to chime in and say that &amp;quot;objectively immoral&amp;quot; is a meaningless expression in terms of Exalted-the-published-setting. The game explicitly and overtly rejects objective morality. <br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> But the game is not going to decide for you what's right and what's wrong, nor how to resolve moral complexities and ethical dilemmas.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good stance. It makes the game work.<br /> <br /> It applies to demon summoning, which is complex, nuanced, exploitative, and as widely accepted by the cultures in Creation as human slavery.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm out. I've made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics\">my case in favour of demon summoning</a> and my case <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-%E2%80%93-john-doe%E2%80%99s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e\">against</a> demon summoning (as an ethical issue) <i>on this forum</i>.<br /> <br /> I stand by what I wrote and have nothing else to say. So I'm out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T01:13:10-07:00","id":1404725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404713#post1404713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, you'll note, that even in 1e an Abyssal could then try and weasel out of that decision. While redemption wasn't given mechanics until 2e, an Abyssal ultimately possesses free will, meaning that an Abyssal who accepts the Mask of Winters' offer, learns his plans, and then defects and tells a circle of Solars what he learned from the Deathlord will have tangibly done <i>vastly more good</i> than the <i>prospective</i> Abyssal who told the Black Exaltation to go fuck itself when the Maiden of Endings came a-knocking.<br /> <br /> \u200bHeck, he's even depriving the Mask of an Abyssal <i>to the same extent</i> as the so-called &quot;moral&quot; refuser.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, so I have been working a bunch and came back to see some heavy stuff. For 3e I'm not going to condemn any particular abyssal for choosing the black exaltation without knowing the reason behind that choice, but don't you think you are being a little hostile here? 'So called' as if someone refusing a deal they may suspect as bad or choosing to meet their appointed fate with dignity instead of railing against it makes them bad or a hypocrite. As if only excepting the power and choosing to defy the Deathlord is right or noble. I respect your belief that that's a good and moral choice but please don't disrespect others who might see refusal as the right choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T02:37:44-07:00","id":1404734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404612#post1404612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I was asked what the UCS thinks about demon summoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pardon my chiming in without taking in full context. {raised hands, nodded head}<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In Exalted it's much less clear if it's good or bad.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> The book entitled &quot;The Realm&quot; contains the lines &quot;slavery is inherently traumatic&quot; and &quot;a happy slave is a broken slave&quot;.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T02:48:38-07:00","id":1404737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404724#post1404724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until you consider Resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resonance is not going to be part of Abyssals anymore. They will have the Great Curse and Limit Breaks.<br /> <br /> I infer that this will somewhat entail dropping the angle of &quot;the Abyssal gradually and inevitably accrues bad juju for acting in a manner contrary to the wishes of Deathlords&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T02:59:30-07:00","id":1404739,"title":"","content":"I keep thinking about the Exaltation of the Abyssals, and I'm drawn to the notion of framing it less as being offered a Faustian bargain and more like, well, the knighting ceremony for the Deathknights.<br /> <br /> Like, sure it still appears before people that have been grievously wounded (although I think it can be written in future to be a bit broader than that), but that could be framed in terms of a person being in the necessary state for approach rather than a vulnerable moment in which they're tricked. They are prostrate in the presence of a figure that would be their liege.<br /> <br /> There is an oath that is offered to service to a liege and an ideal standard of behaviour, as knights were offered, and sure it includes references to the rewards for proper service (which in this case does manage to include life). For the one that pledges themselves to that oath, a kiss and a punch in the face, and maybe that angle could be made heavier by modifying with other mythic rebirth imagery; run through with a spear of ash, hung by a noose, drowned, frozen, struck by a bolt from the black sky. However you are struck, you arise a knight.<br /> <br /> Is the Abyssal bound by their oath? I think that needs to be considered in terms of a world where we might assume that people on the whole take oaths a bit more seriously. That might at least take the form of requiring them to form an elaborate justification for breaking the terms of the oath with reference to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T04:09:57-07:00","id":1404746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404677#post1404677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, they don't. One of the intrinsic properties of goodness is a respect for life; likewise the lawful alignment aligns itself with order and justice. Murder is against both of those things, so even if Saint Cuthbert <i>wants you to</i> break into the Asmodeus cultist mayor's manor and stove in his head while he's sleeping, that won't make it Lawful Good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we agree that, in the context of DD, it can be considered loyal good to lawfully execute a terrible criminal ? If no, we don't agree about some core premises of DD (which I may be wrong about). If yes, I think you see my and JohnDoe244 point clearly enough but we are arguing over technicalities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T04:43:55-07:00","id":1404749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404746#post1404746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do we agree that, in the context of DD, it can be considered loyal good to lawfully execute a terrible criminal ? If no, we don't agree about some core premises of DD (which I may be wrong about). If yes, I think you see my and JohnDoe244 point clearly enough but we are arguing over technicalities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly no, I don't agree. Killing people can be the most effective, best answer, but that doesn't make it the *good* answer. Murder is often a *very* effective solution when sentient beings are being problems. That doesn't mean that you aren't killing someone, and ending all chance of them ever having a positive effect on the world. Nor does killing them erase the damage they've already done.<br /> <br /> The Lawful Good Knight still executes the criminal, but that is because they lack access to an option that is more effective *and* ethically superior. The lawful good knight shouldn't *feel good* about executing the criminal, though they might still because, yknow, flawed human beings and whatnot.<br /> <br /> And, heck, in the context of exalted there are *very* few beings you can't, eventually, talk around to being *better.* So. It's not even that great a solution to just kill them, *anyway.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23941,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","user":"Aquatica","date":".  thanks computer just cut off half my sentence, cool. 07-26-2020, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","name":"Aquatica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T05:49:42-07:00","id":1404759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404725#post1404725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but don't you think you are being a little hostile here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not one of the people in this thread telling people that the morally superior thing to do in a situation is <i>to stop being alive</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200bTelling someone the world would be better off if they died, that's pretty hostile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 'So called' as if someone refusing a deal they may suspect as bad or choosing to meet their appointed fate with dignity instead of railing against it makes them bad or a hypocrite. </div> </div> </div>The person who sacrifices herself is not a hypocrite; the person who <i>tells others</i> to sacrifice themselves while they remain comfortably alive, however, is worth questioning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As if only excepting the power and choosing to defy the Deathlord is right or noble. </div> </div> </div>It's not the <i>only </i>right choice, no, but it's <i>a</i> right choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T07:27:30-07:00","id":1404768,"title":"","content":"My issue with Abyssals having 'original sin' simply by choosing to live is that I found it got in the way of more tangible regrets and moments where they realised their Deathlords weren't to be trusted.<br /> <br /> &quot;I've realised that the Lover Clad doesn't really care about me... in retrospect the part where I agreed to help her destroy the world was kind of a red flag, but in my defence the sex was really great.&quot; <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T07:39:34-07:00","id":1404772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404749#post1404749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly no, I don't agree. Killing people can be the most effective, best answer, but that doesn't make it the *good* answer. Murder is often a *very* effective solution when sentient beings are being problems. That doesn't mean that you aren't killing someone, and ending all chance of them ever having a positive effect on the world. Nor does killing them erase the damage they've already done.<br /> <br /> The Lawful Good Knight still executes the criminal, but that is because they lack access to an option that is more effective *and* ethically superior. The lawful good knight shouldn't *feel good* about executing the criminal, though they might still because, yknow, flawed human beings and whatnot.<br /> <br /> And, heck, in the context of exalted there are *very* few beings you can't, eventually, talk around to being *better.* So. It's not even that great a solution to just kill them, *anyway.*</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, I'm talking in context of DD. In the Exalted Deeds, Zaphkiel, the god who preside over all that is good, has in its description <span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:CelestiaAntiqua\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Zaphkiel embodies the perfect good, and only the most exalted creatures can stand in his presence without being consumed.&quot; That makes no damn sense, but this guy is still some sort of divine incarnation of the Lawful Good alignment.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to solve what is good or not in every game, but trying to argue that in the world of DD, &quot;good&quot; has a very peculiar sense (that not everyone agrees on within the same universe, most likely). But in the DD game series, from my experience and my readings, many acts we would consider foolish or evil are good. Or at least, Good.<br /> <br /> All that to say that I support the idea that the &quot;laws of ethics&quot; vary depending the game you are playing in (I'm supporting JohnDoe244 position). (Or, the era and place you are living in on earth, even more simply).</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T07:39:54-07:00","id":1404773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404759#post1404759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not one of the people in this thread telling people that the morally superior thing to do in a situation is <i>to stop being alive</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200bTelling someone the world would be better off if they died, that's pretty hostile.<br /> <br /> The person who sacrifices herself is not a hypocrite; the person who <i>tells others</i> to sacrifice themselves while they remain comfortably alive, however, is worth questioning.<br /> <br /> It's not the <i>only </i>right choice, no, but it's <i>a</i> right choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be perfectly clear, I'm not attacking you Alucard, merely curious at the tone of your post. I agree on the first point, your second point requires particular examples as the situations behind exaltation are fluid,condemning someone for choosing to ally with a Deathlord without understanding the situation is ignorant but doesn't necessarily imply intent for you to sacrifice yourself. As for your third, yes I agree with you, my wording was to be objective, I stated I respect your belief but I also believe it to be morally acceptable. My objection is to the ridicule I felt the so called moral person part of your statement implies to someone who decided to say no to the Deathlord. I see that as an acceptable choice as well. I'm sorry if it seems I'm picking on you in particular but taking John doe as an example, his posts don't seem deviate from his normal manner and yours seemed emotionally charged in the negative. We're all here to have fun and everyone should at least try and be cordial and respect others believe even if they don't match our own( to an extent anyway, if a person has monstrous beliefs we should just ignore them until the moderators deal with them causingproblems). This includes you of course, your beliefs are to be respected and I hope you don't feel the I don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","user":"Arkayriel","date":".  Missed an important word - seem 07-26-2020, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T08:00:22-07:00","id":1404776,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24445\" data-vbnamecard=\"24445\">Arkayriel</a> It's starting to become a long thread, but take a look back. I might be &quot;emotionally charged in the negative,&quot; but I wasn't the one invoking transphobia, filicide, or the Holocaust to mess with the heads of people I'm having a discussion with.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's awfully hard to &quot;have fun&quot; with that taking place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-26-2020, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T08:03:19-07:00","id":1404777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404768#post1404768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue with Abyssals having 'original sin' simply by choosing to live is that I found it got in the way of more tangible regrets and moments where they realised their Deathlords weren't to be trusted.<br /> <br /> &quot;I've realised that the Lover Clad doesn't really care about me... in retrospect the part where I agreed to help her destroy the world was kind of a red flag, but in my defence the sex was really great.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>True and to be fair it ruins something reaaallly important, they're fucking Exalted! Yeah it's twisted and tied to death, but it's the power of legendary heroes that do the impossible and spit in Fate's eye. If they wanna be evil, fine. Look at the Solars, they had plenty horrible monsters and they were supposed to be the champions of righteousness.<br /> <br /> And if they want to be good? Then the Deathlords better watch out cuz that Deathknight needs some new simulated plate. Just...you know... Close your eyes of you're squeamish cuz Abyssal powers are still very vicious, that fight ain't gonna.be pretty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T08:30:39-07:00","id":1404778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404776#post1404776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24445\" data-vbnamecard=\"24445\">Arkayriel</a> It's starting to become a long thread, but take a look back. I might be &quot;emotionally charged in the negative,&quot; but I wasn't the one invoking transphobia, filicide, or the Holocaust to dunk on people I'm having a discussion with.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's awfully hard to &quot;have fun&quot; with that taking place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep and I somehow missed the post where you explained how words were being put in your mouth, seems you were coming under heavy fire. Regardless of whether I agree with all of your elements of not I understand now why you seemed hostile. I was wondering if you were intentionally taking a shot at someone or focusing your ire on anyone who disagreed with you. My apologies, I didn't mean to join a dogpile. It's a shame that A) I have to go to bed now and so can't continue and B) both sides of the debate have been agitated to a point where I can offer little meaningful to the conversation that won't cause more problems. I will risk a quick statement however.<br /> <br /> Life's greatest instinct is to live. To that end all the niceties and societal mores go out the window when ones very existence is on the line. It takes incredible integrity to sacrifice oneself when there is any way to justify the choice to live. I'm not saying I have the ability to know that would be the right call or wrong call, I know I don't have the wisdom to judge someone in that situation fairly. I do believe it's wrong to blanket an entire group under the statement of they're evil, without examining their particulars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T08:45:24-07:00","id":1404782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404778#post1404778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying I have the ability to know that would be the right call or wrong call, I know I don't have the wisdom to judge someone in that situation fairly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you and I don't have a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T11:11:54-07:00","id":1404808,"title":"","content":"By the way, let me just say that I've missed threads like this.<br /> <br /> My battery is running out, but I look forward to seeing where this discussion goes next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T13:56:37-07:00","id":1404829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404808#post1404808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I look forward to seeing where this discussion goes next.</div> </div> </div> </div>Preferably more Jen art.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T15:49:03-07:00","id":1404837,"title":"","content":"I also want to point out that it's pretty normal for ritualistic behavior to invoke hyperbole for purposes of a compelling mythic narrative. Peasants compelled to swear fealty unto death to their liege lord or whatever may or may not see that oath as genuinely binding, especially if they're only doing it because they have to, in order to keep living where they do, and also everyone else they know has done the same thing and hardly anyone has ever been expected to give their life as a result. When the skeleton in the robe with the scythe magically stops time for you at the moment of death in order to offer you a second chance and unfathomable powers to go with it <i>but only</i> on the condition that you accept your fate from that moment forth will be to carry within you the inevitable death of all things, the extent to which you characterize that as &quot;real&quot; and the extent to which you characterize it as some ritual hokum you have dance through in order to come out the other side with this skeleton guy as a patron is going to vary depending on to what extent you've previously inhabited a set of social norms where &quot;navigating ritual hyperbole and mouthing magic words due to social pressure&quot; is just the Done Thing in order to keep living your life. And, honestly, most of us inhabit social norms where that's a thing. That's pretty normal! Exalted even has it in its rules that you don't need to feel anything in your heart in order for your ritual propitiation to count as worship for purposes of empowering a god through prayer!<br /> <br /> And I know previous editions have occasionally been insistent on something like &quot;You need to truly accept it deep in your heart and not just mouth the words in order to make the magic go&quot; or &quot;Part of the magic working imposes the profound knowledge of the true nature of the oath deep in your heart!&quot; but, like, that is so outside the realm of real human experience. Do we need that? Really? Can't we just accept that it's normal for folks to get in over their head in a way that they ought to be able to look back on and go &quot;Wow, I should have been paying attention to the words coming out of my mouth&quot;?<br /> <br /> (Also contracts made under threat of death can't be ethically binding.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 07-26-2020, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T16:15:56-07:00","id":1404839,"title":"","content":"A few weeks ago, I came upon this blog called A Collection of Unmitigated Pedantry. It's this history professor who gives his own take on things related to pop culture depictions of ancient and Medieval history, both in terms of specific examples and general abstractions. It's pretty good, very detailed but not impenetrably so, and it often strikes a fair balance between pointing out what fiction gets wrong (and right) and acknowledgement that fiction has its own necessities.<br /> <br /> Probably his landmark thing are these multi-entry breakdowns of the siege of Minas Tirith and battle of the Hornburg in Lord of the Rings (including comparisons between their depictions in book and film). I also rather like his take down of myths for the Spartans. He's recently putting up the first in a series of entries about the historical manufacture of bread.<br /> <br /> It's a pretty good blog, I recommend it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, right now my perspective on how people might regard an oath underlying their induction as a deathknight is in his article about the composition and connotations of Medieval oaths.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://acoup.blog/2019/06/28/collections-oaths-how-do-they-work/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/acoup.blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/1280px-bayeux_tapestry_scene23_harold_sacramentum_fecit_willelmo_duci.jpg?fit=1200%2C819&amp;ssl=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://acoup.blog/2019/06/28/collections-oaths-how-do-they-work/\" target=\"_blank\"> Collections: Oaths! How do they Work? </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://acoup.blog/2019/06/28/collections-oaths-how-do-they-work/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://acoup.blog/2019/06/28/collections-oaths-how-do-they-work/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> By popular request, today we&rsquo;re going to talk about oaths. Oaths appear a lot in fantasy fiction &ndash; and even in historical fiction &ndash; and they are frequently done wrong. I remarked &hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It compels me to... interrogate certain perspectives that might seem to draw a distinction between what is real and what is ritual hokum in a manner that might be a tad too modern revisionist. It reminds me of when people lean on arguments about the Crusades that try to find more pragmatic, materialist reasons for why they happen, sceptical of the idea that people really would travel hundreds of miles and engage in warfare at great expense primarily for religious convictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T16:34:07-07:00","id":1404841,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth noting that the Silver Prince is genuinely a better ruler than most of the actual living rulers, with a higher quality of life for those within his domain, a clear upward momentum for those in the lower classes and a plan for expansion that doesn't involve violent means. And in 3e they've stated they're dropping the &quot;actually a front for a soulteel navy&quot; tagline and just having him focus on a cultural victory. And this dude is a freaking deathlord. So the &quot;all abyssals are absolutely evil&quot; line is sort of a dying attitude in the game going forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T18:03:33-07:00","id":1404853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404839#post1404839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few weeks ago, I came upon this blog called A Collection of Unmitigated Pedantry. It's this history professor who gives his own take on things related to pop culture depictions of ancient and Medieval history, both in terms of specific examples and general abstractions. It's pretty good, very detailed but not impenetrably so, and it often strikes a fair balance between pointing out what fiction gets wrong (and right) and acknowledgement that fiction has its own necessities.<br /> <br /> Probably his landmark thing are these multi-entry breakdowns of the siege of Minas Tirith and battle of the Hornburg in Lord of the Rings (including comparisons between their depictions in book and film). I also rather like his take down of myths for the Spartans. He's recently putting up the first in a series of entries about the historical manufacture of bread.<br /> <br /> It's a pretty good blog, I recommend it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, right now my perspective on how people might regard an oath underlying their induction as a deathknight is in his article about the composition and connotations of Medieval oaths.<br /> <a href=\"https://acoup.blog/2019/06/28/collections-oaths-how-do-they-work/\" target=\"_blank\">https://acoup.blog/2019/06/28/collec...-do-they-work/</a><br /> <br /> It compels me to... interrogate certain perspectives that might seem to draw a distinction between what is real and what is ritual hokum in a manner that might be a tad too modern revisionist. It reminds me of when people lean on arguments about the Crusades that try to find more pragmatic, materialist reasons for why they happen, sceptical of the idea that people really would travel hundreds of miles and engage in warfare at great expense primarily for religious convictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything in that article is accurate, but I'm strongly influenced here by the works of James C. Scott and his take on peasant ethics and their position on their place in the social order, which is, uh, complex, but which for the purpose of this post I guess I'm going to sum up as &quot;They take it as valid while also recognizing how bullshit it is enough to confabulate reasons for why they ought to be able to violate it when they need to, or why certain social obliations don't count when they become inconvenient for them personally or collectively.&quot; I also think things like priesthoods and knightly orders self-select for a degree of ideological devotion, but Deathlords looking for Deathknight candidates don't have that luxury, because they have to look for hypothetical Solar Exaltation candidates on the verge of death, which are going to be more evenly distributed across the population and thus you're going to get less of the sort of people who self select for going on crusade and more for people who subscribe to peasant ethics, which make up a substantially greater percentage of the population.<br /> <br /> I think you're probably going to get a lot of True Believers among the ranks of the Deathknights, but it's less about fully pledging themselves to the cause of the Neverborn at the moment of Exaltation as some sort of original sin you can judge Abyssal Exalted by collectively, and more the effects of subsequent training and indoctrination once they're taken under their patrons' tutelage.<br /> <br /> (Deathlords'll totes use &quot;You were damned to kill the world the moment you took your Second Breath&quot; as a talking point during that indoctrination, tho!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 07-26-2020, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T19:59:20-07:00","id":1404869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404601#post1404601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have another essay about the difference between moral systems that draw a categorical line between non-sexual and sexual violence and coercion and those that don't, but I don't know how dark I want to get here.</div> </div> </div> </div>For whatever it\u2019s worth I would be very interested in reading this if you decide on an appropriate place to post it. The moral distinction on fall back on tends to be \u201clook there are specific types of violence people at the game table are statistically more likely to have experienced and not disclosed than others, and I\u2019m going to be extra cautious with those types\u201d and would be very interested in reading a stronger in-world ethical distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T20:34:45-07:00","id":1404871,"title":"","content":"The discussion has somewhat moved on, but in regard to the 3E form of elemental summoning: In Jainism, minute ensouled beings are constantly taking birth and dying. When you so much as strike a match you are bringing a conscious being into the world who will live and die for only a few seconds. While in Jain theology such a being has and will eventually be a human, Exalted isn't quite that inclusive in the cycle of souls. Still, it is relatively easy to construct an internally consistent moral position that conforms with both real world and in-setting morals which permits creating a being for the express purpose of performing a service for you as part of its cycle of spiritual growth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404739#post1404739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Abyssal bound by their oath? I think that needs to be considered in terms of a world where we might assume that people on the whole take oaths a bit more seriously. That might at least take the form of requiring them to form an elaborate justification for breaking the terms of the oath with reference to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potentially important is the fact that traditional oaths include both a supernatural guarantor and the punishment of faithlessness. Christianity caused those features to atrophy because the guarantor was always God and the punishment was always eternal damnation. That which was theologically obvious could be left unstated.<br /> <br /> Edit: My own fault for replying before I got to the end of the thread. I see you and I have both found that blog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 07-26-2020, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T21:15:32-07:00","id":1404874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404869#post1404869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For whatever it\u2019s worth I would be very interested in reading this if you decide on an appropriate place to post it. The moral distinction on fall back on tends to be \u201clook there are specific types of violence people at the game table are statistically more likely to have experienced and not disclosed than others, and I\u2019m going to be extra cautious with those types\u201d and would be very interested in reading a stronger in-world ethical distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what, I'll just do the simple version:<br /> <br /> Consider, in an individual in power, the interaction between an ethical system where sexual violence/coersion is <i>worse but not categorically distinct</i> from non-sexual violence/coersion, and an ethical system where it is possible for an individual to opt-out (or be forcibly opted out via the actions of their antecedents) from consideration re: &quot;Is violence against this individual unjust?&quot;<br /> <br /> (In practical terms, at the table and probably when writing books, you want to make sure all your NPCs are running on an ethical system where sexual violence is not just worse than non-sexual violence but is categorically distinct, even though this is probably anachronistic to many of the setting's foundational genre inspirations.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 07-27-2020, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T22:53:26-07:00","id":1404880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404874#post1404874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know what, I'll just do the simple version:<br /> <br /> Consider, in an individual in power, the interaction between an ethical system where sexual violence/coersion is <i>worse but not categorically distinct</i> from non-sexual violence/coersion, and an ethical system where it is possible for an individual to opt-out (or be forcibly opted out via the actions of their antecedents) from consideration re: &amp;quot;Is violence against this individual unjust?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> (In practical terms, at the table and probably when writing books, you want to make sure all your NPCs are running on an ethical system where sexual violence is not just worse than non-sexual violence but is categorically distinct, even though this is probably anachronistic to many of the setting's foundational genre inspirations.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a hard time seeing how a full in-setting distinction can be drawn once a setting incorporates full fledged chattel slavery though. I\u2019m not defending rape as plot device at the game table! Just saying it\u2019s something I have to hand wave as not coming up more often then actually presenting it as unthinkable for Dynast or Guild npcs in-setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T02:40:08-07:00","id":1404896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403985-hello-there-sir-can-i-get-the-consent-paper-for-your-sex-slaves-plz-~?p=1404871#post1404871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The discussion has somewhat moved on, but in regard to the 3E form of elemental summoning: In Jainism, minute ensouled beings are constantly taking birth and dying. When you so much as strike a match you are bringing a conscious being into the world who will live and die for only a few seconds. While in Jain theology such a being has and will eventually be a human, Exalted isn't quite that inclusive in the cycle of souls. Still, it is relatively easy to construct an internally consistent moral position that conforms with both real world and in-setting morals which permits creating a being for the express purpose of performing a service for you as part of its cycle of spiritual growth.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one I like. It's a simple yet effective way of explaining summoning stuff out of nowhere and integrating it fully into the setting, with a positive moral justification. As JohnDoe244 has taught me : Yoink !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}